          "file": "scripts/system-pulse/gpu_capture.py",
          "line": 182
        }
      ],
      "trigger": "An original start-record failure or actual SIGINT occurs, then a stream context exit raises EIO.",
      "expected": "Raise the original exception object and retain the stream-close error separately.",
      "actual": "The outer except runs after context exits, assigns the close error as primary, and raises it; capture_errors is empty. The original survives only in __context__. All owned processes are nevertheless reaped/absent.",
      "impact": "Violates the Q1 primary/secondary error contract and misidentifies the failure/cancellation in compact capture records; no new process leak or false acceptance demonstrated.",
      "remedy": "Capture execution errors before stream closure, close each stream through a guarded secondary-error path, preserve the first exception object and keep unconditional bounded process cleanup. Add combined ENOSPC/close and SIGINT/close regressions with a close-only control.",
